  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200b;&#x200b;Humanitarian Response to People in Situations of Mobility, Transit, and Displacement in Honduras in the Context of Insecurity and Humanitarian Crises &#x200b;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In light of the increased risks experienced in Honduras as a result of disasters, risky migration, food insecurity and widespread violence among many other factors which are interrelated, IOM with the help of implementing partners (Plan International Honduras, Honduran Red Cross, and Fundaci&#xf3;n Alivio del Sufrimiento) is responding to the essential needs of populations on the move (internally displaced, returnees, migrants in mixed flows) through a multisectoral response including Camp Coordination and Camp Management, Shelter/Non-Food Items, and Multi-Purpose Cash assistance. Additionally, the project is contributing to the protection of people affected by disasters or displacement by providing temporary accommodation that also offers access to essential services and household items in a dignified manner. This project follows the approach of centrality of protection, accountability to affected people, protection against sexual exploitation and abuse, inclusion of people with disabilities, mainstreaming of gender and age considerations.</narrative>
  </description>
